      "Reinforce the point that 'trône' derived from Early Modern French 'throsne' (preconsonantal /s/ amuissement) and quote Littré's direct refutation of the 'majesté' myth.",
      "Reiterate that 'dôme' (from Classical Latin 'domus') and 'môle' (from Latin 'moles') never had an /s/ in French and were given circumflexes in 18th-century codification solely to prescribe closed [o], making Option C fully attested in French orthographic practice.",
